  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The passive with -ся",
     "texto": [
      "With imperfective verbs that take a direct object, **-ся** is added to the verb: **строить** → **строится** («is built»), **покупать** → **покупается** («is bought»), **продавать** → **продаётся** («is sold»).",
      "The object becomes the subject: **Книги продаются здесь** («books are sold here»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Past and future",
     "texto": [
      "With the imperfective, **-ся** presents the process: **Дом строился три года** («the house was being built for three years»). To indicate that it was completed, the perfective is usually used: **Дом построили за три года** («they built the house in three years»).",
      "The future **будет строиться** expresses a future process; **дорогу построят** indicates that they will build the road and expect to finish it. To name the agent, use the active: **Эту школу строит известная компания** («This school is being built by a well-known company»)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
